<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>fmc third-party licenses</title></head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party licenses</h1>
<p>fmc includes the following third-party software.</p>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
{{#each licenses}}
<h2 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h2>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}  <li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</li>
{{/each}}</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
<h2 id="vendored-grammars">Vendored grammars</h2>
<p>fmc compiles these tree-sitter parsers from <code>vendor/grammars/</code> into the binary. Each one is built from the upstream commit named here, and its licence applies to that code.</p>
<ul>
<li>vimdoc: <a href="https://github.com/neovim/tree-sitter-vimdoc">neovim/tree-sitter-vimdoc</a> at cf5f03718e699c0e37e4f26a4417fb744c714ba2, Apache-2.0 (the Apache-2.0 text is in its entry above).</li>
<li>just: <a href="https://github.com/casey/tree-sitter-just">casey/tree-sitter-just</a> at 5685543a6e64f66335e25518c9ae8ffa1dae3d01, Apache-2.0 by its LICENSE file (its Cargo.toml says MIT). The Apache-2.0 text is in its entry above.</li>
<li>luadoc: <a href="https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-luadoc">tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-luadoc</a> at 4d04632a3a398b78af52e83be074883e722f40be, MIT.</li>
<li>luap: <a href="https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-luap">tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-luap</a> at c134aaec6acf4fa95fe4aa0dc9aba3eacdbbe55a, MIT.</li>
</ul>
